            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: What is the process for installing a commercial asphalt parking lot in Concord, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates conducts site elevation surveying, excavates organic topsoil, and installs a 6-to-10 inch dense-graded crushed gravel base. Teams apply a 2-inch MassDOT binder course followed by a 1.5-inch dense top coat of hot-mix asphalt, compacted using heavy vibratory rollers. S. Phaneuf & Associates completes the parking lot installation with extruded asphalt Cape Cod berms, catch basin tie-ins, and thermal pavement striping compliant with Concord municipal codes.</p>

            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: How does S. Phaneuf & Associates design retaining walls in Concord to resist winter frost-heave?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates excavates a base trench below the local frost line (36 to 42 inches deep) and backfills with a 12-inch layer of angular crushed stone. Masons construct the retaining wall using interlocking concrete blocks or natural New England fieldstone, incorporating continuous perforated drain pipes wrapped in filter fabric behind the wall structure. This engineering releases hydrostatic pressure and prevents ice expansion from pushing retaining walls out of alignment during Concord winters.</p>
